within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.D_Dermatologicals.D11A_OtherDermatologicalPreparations.D11AH05_Dupilumab;
model Dupilumab_Briggs2023_PD_easi
  "indirect_response_i exposure-response sweep — Briggs_2023 :: EASI (Eczema Area and Severity Index (EASI))"
  extends Pharmacolibrary.Interfaces.PartialExposureResponseSweep(
    E0 = 30.4,      // [units]
    Emax = 0.266,  // type I effect term
    EC50 = 0.0203,  // [kg/m3; mg/L × 0.001]
    gamma = 1,
    exposure_per_s = 0.001);   // 1 mg/L per second
equation
  response = E0*(1 - Emax*frac);   // steady state, indirect response type I
  // defaulted: gamma
  annotation(experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 210, Interval = 0.42),
    Documentation(info = "<html><body><h4>Dupilumab_Briggs2023_PD_easi</h4><p>The steady-state exposure-response curve of Briggs E et al., <i>Pharmaceutical research 40(11):2653–2666</i> 2023 (<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1007/s11095-023-03616-8\">doi:10.1007/s11095-023-03616-8</a>) — Eczema Area and Severity Index (EASI) [units] against dupilumab mg/L — obtained by sweeping the driver instead of simulating a dose. Model family: indirect_response_i.</p><h4>The parameters, in the paper's terms</h4><pre>  E0    =       30.4 units    drug-free response (baseline) (Baseline EASI score units, Q324)
  Emax  =      0.266          maximal effect term (Drug effect (Imax), Q323)
  EC50  =       20.3 mg/L     exposure at half of the maximal effect term (IC50 (mg/L), Q322)
  gamma = (library default) Hill coefficient</pre><p>The algebra is <code>response = E0*(1 - Emax*frac)</code>; this model only supplies the numbers. The x axis is one mg/L of dupilumab per second of simulated time (exposure is in kg/m3): there is no state, no dose and no kinetics — plot <code>response</code> against <code>exposure</code> (or <code>time</code>).</p><h4>What it reproduces</h4><pre>  exposure = 0         response 30.4   (drug-free)
  exposure = EC50 (20.3 mg/L)  response 26.36
  exposure -> infinity  response 22.31</pre></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Briggs_2023: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: accepted with caveats</li></ul></body></html>"));
end Dupilumab_Briggs2023_PD_easi;
